 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance of\nnon-commercial drivers' licenses and learners' permits",
    "basePrintNo": "S6584",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6584-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§201 & 502, V & T L (as proposed in S.1747-B & A.3675-B)",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6584\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to the issuance of non-commercial drivers' licenses and lear-\nners' permits\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo clarify provisions of a Chapter of the Laws of 2019 relating to the\nissuance of drivers' licenses and learners' permits that do not meet\nfederal standards for identification.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends a provision prohibiting the Department of Motor Vehi-\ncles from disclosing (1) original documents or copies of documents\ncollected from non-commercial driver's license or learner's permit\napplicants or (2) any record that identifies whether the type of driv-\ner's license or learner's permit a person holds either meets or does not\nmeet federal standards for identification, to make an exception as\nrequired for the Department to process an application or renewal appli-\ncation for a driver's license or learner's permit that meets federal\nstandards for identification. This section also amends a provision\nrelating to a mandatory notice requirement to clarify that the notice\nrequirement would not apply if prohibited by a lawful court order or\nfederal judicial warrant.\n\nSection two clarifies a provision prohibiting an application form for a\ndriver's license or learner's permit which does not meet federal stand-\nards for identification from stating an applicant's citizenship or immi-\ngration status, by providing an exception as required to comply with the\nNational Voter Registration Act of 1993.\n\nSection three provides that this act shall take effect on the same date\nas a chapter of the laws of 2019, as proposed in legislative bills\nS.1747-8 and A.3675-B, takes effect.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:  /sl 1 This legislation is necessary to clarify certain\nprovisions in the \"Driver's License Access and Privacy Act\" that relate\nto procedures that are required to process the applications of individ-\nuals applying for drivers' licenses and learners' permits that meet\nfederal standards for identification, and the state's conformance with\nthe National Voter Registration Act of 1993.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2019, amending the vehicle and traffic law relat-\ning to the issuance of non-commercial drivers' licenses and learners'\npermits; and to repeal certain provisions of such law relating to driv-\ner's license applications, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n1747-B and A. 3675B, takes effect.\n",
